<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'Elastic Beanstalk Deployment'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>Application Deployment with Elastic Beanstalk</h1>
  <p>Deployed and managed a sample Tomcat application using AWS Elastic Beanstalk, learning how PaaS simplifies infrastructure management.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Elastic Beanstalk</span><span>EC2</span><span>PaaS</span><span>Tomcat</span><span>Auto Scaling</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/beanstalk.png" alt="Elastic Beanstalk Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>In this project, I used <strong>AWS Elastic Beanstalk</strong> to deploy a <strong>sample Tomcat application</strong>. Beanstalk automates provisioning, scaling, and monitoring — letting developers focus on code while AWS manages infrastructure.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>⚙️ Beanstalk Managed</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EC2 Instances</strong> — Run the Tomcat app</li>
          <li><strong>Security Group</strong> — HTTP/SSH access control</li>
          <li><strong>IAM Role</strong> — AWSElasticBeanstalkWebTier</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>📊 Monitoring</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CloudWatch</strong> — Health and logs</li>
          <li><strong>Load Balancer</strong> — Optional traffic distribution</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Understood how Beanstalk <strong>abstracts infrastructure management</strong>.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>IAM roles</strong> for Beanstalk environments.</li>
      <li>Experienced deploying an app <strong>without writing CloudFormation or Terraform</strong>.</li>
      <li>Monitored health status and accessed <strong>app logs</strong> directly from Beanstalk.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <strong>custom domains with Route 53</strong> and HTTPS certificates in production.</li>
      <li>Enable <strong>Multi-AZ with Auto Scaling</strong> for high availability.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>Amazon RDS</strong> instead of local DB for the data layer.</li>
      <li>Integrate <strong>CI/CD pipelines</strong> for automated deployments.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

